# Conservative EAS Build exclusions (Build 9). Only excludes directories confirmed to have NO
# runtime import/require from src/ (grepped before adding each entry) -- never anything the
# Expo app actually bundles or needs at build time.
#
# IMPORTANT -- see the Build 9 final report for the real finding: these exclusions are small
# (well under 1MB combined). The actual EAS archive bulk (~236MB of the ~239MB working tree)
# is the assets/creatures*/ family, which this file deliberately does NOT exclude -- most of
# that is still statically require()'d by the still-registered /creature-lab route
# (src/app/creature-lab.tsx -> src/data/creature-lab/creature-assets.ts), so excluding it here
# would break the Metro bundle, not just shrink it. That is a product/code decision (retiring
# an R&D-only route), not a build-config change, and is explicitly flagged for review rather
# than acted on in this pass.

# Documentation -- never imported by app code.
docs/
*.md

# Validation/QA scripts -- run via `npx tsx scripts/validate-*.ts` locally/in CI, never
# imported by the Expo app itself.
scripts/

# Supabase project (migrations, Edge Functions, local config) -- deployed separately via the
# Supabase CLI; never part of the Expo client bundle.
supabase/

# Standard non-build-artifact excludes.
.git/
.vscode/
